The Space Force & Air Force IT Division has an immediate opening for a Senior Financial Analyst. This role will support an array of complexities within the division, including: Programs/task orders that span multiple sectors; financial reporting and briefings to division, business area, and sector leadership; direct interaction and collaboration with external customers; and new business analysis with a focus on business case development. Under the leadership of the Division Finance & Business Operations Senior Manager, you will be challenged to identify and development innovative solutions that drives the division meeting and exceeding the financial metric targets. 

Primary Tasks:

Support monthly EACs in close coordination with finance and program teams, including in-depth variance and trend analysis;

Prepare, communicate, and present complex financial forecasts with various elements of cost and various competition types;

Work with program management to identify risks and opportunities that will impact program financials as well as potential mitigation measures as appropriate;

Develop road maps for path to closure on financial targets;

Develop innovative solutions/processes that improve either the division capabilities or financial position;

Work closely with other functional areas such as the contracts team, subcontractor team, etc. on financial related elements;

Work month-end closing processes including variance/trend analysis, with focus on operational activities impacting the financial results;

Support the consolidation of division finances, including the preparation and development of monthly operating review packages;

Ability to clearly and articulately communicate with Division, Business Area, and Sector leadership;

Support the annual operating plan development, including pipeline reviews and long range planning;

Provide New Business analysis and build out of business case scenarios;

Support Service Center budgeting, allocations, and variance analysis;

Provide as needed training of junior financial analyst within the division

Basic Qualifications:

Bachelor’s Degree in Finance, Business Administration, or a related discipline and 12+ years of experience related to program financial control or or Masters with 10 – 13 years of prior relevant experience.

Familiar with multiple contract types such as CPAF, FFP, and T&M

Knowledge of service center management and forecasting

Detail oriented, independent worker, with strong attention to detail and accuracy

Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, PowerPoint, Word) skills

US citizenship

Preferred Qualifications:

Experience with Leidos financial systems and processes: Costpoint, Fusion, Deltek, PowerBI

Strong knowledge and experience in financial reporting out of Hyperion products (SmartView)

Excel expertise and proficiency with PowerPoint presentations

Government contracting industry experience


